               DIGITAL'S PARTNERING INITIATIVES DRIVE
                   ADVANCED CLIENT/SERVER SOFTWARE


   ...Alliances, Expanded Channels Add Value, Choice for Users...
      Offerings Accelerate Customer Migration to Client/Server
                             Computing...


MAYNARD, Mass. -- September 29, 1994 -- Digital Equipment 
Corporation today announced agreements with Computer Associates, 
Inc., and Oracle Corporation to package, sell, and service their 
popular database products with Digital's award-winning LinkWorks 
software.  Customers can choose either CA-Ingres or ORACLE7 software 
with LinkWorks in convenient packaging for $499 per user, on 
average, a cost savings of 44 percent from the total price of 
separately purchased components.

     To offer customers an even broader choice of packaged 
databases, Digital and Sybase, Inc., have signed a letter of intent 
to package LinkWorks with Sybase System 10.  The companies expect to 
reach formal agreement next month.

In addition, Digital announced:

     o  Enhanced PATHWORKS for DOS and Windows software.  This is 
        the first network operating system (NOS) to build in the 
        Mosaic graphics navigation tool that lets PC users easily 
        access and browse the Internet's World-Wide Web; the first 
        with client support for mobile and wireless computing that 
        gives portable users the same computing environment they 
        have at the office; and the first to include the foundation 
        that helps customers more easily implement client/server 
        applications in multivendor networks;

     o  New ACCESSWORKS gateways that extend access from 9 to 66 
        databases on a wide range of platforms such as Alpha AXP, 
        VAX, IBM, Hewlett-Packard, Sun Microsystems, and popular 
        personal computers; and

     o  New business practices that provide a simplified software 
        licensing and software pricing structure for Alpha AXP and 
        VAX systems.  The new pricing structure significantly 
        reduces software lifecycle, transaction, and administration 
        costs for information system and local area network 
        managers. 

     "The number of product 'firsts', combined with aggressive 
partnering and simplified business practices in today's 
client/server announcement, reflects the new direction of Digital's 
software business," said Nancy N. Strecker, vice president, Digital 
Software Products.  "We're moving forward quickly to provide 
customers with more product value and more choice in the way they 
buy.  We're making it easier for them to do business with Digital." 

Agreements Give Customers More Choice 

     The LinkWorks/database packages include the runtime version of 
either CA-Ingres or ORACLE7 software plus Digital's LinkWorks 
groupware solution framework, which integrates personal 
productivity, group and business applications to achieve 
departmental and business goals. Digital, Computer Associates, Inc., 
and Oracle Corporation will work with their nearly 6,500 business 
partners to market, deliver, and support value-added LinkWorks 
solutions worldwide.  Service and support will be provided through 
Digital's global Multivendor Customer Services organization.  The 
CA-Ingres package is scheduled for shipment before the end of this  
year.  The ORACLE7 package with LinkWorks is available immediately. 

New Partners Program 

     To further enhance its indirect channels effort, Digital also 
is announcing the LinkWorks Partner Program for VARs, systems
integrators and software developers.  The program provides, at no
cost to partners, LinkWorks and database products for demonstration
and trial use.  Also available are toolkits, technical training, and
sales and marketing support. 

     LinkWorks enables developers to build solutions using the tools 
of their choice, such as Microsoft's Visual Basic or C++.  With the 
new LinkWorks Software Developer's Kit (SDK), developers can easily 
and rapidly modify, extend, and add unique value to their solutions 
and re-use these components to match customer requirements.  The 
LinkWorks SDK will be available this year.  A beta version is 
available today for select "early adopter" partners. 

Powerful PATHWORKS Client/Server Capabilities 

     PATHWORKS for DOS and Windows is the first NOS to ship with the 
Mosaic navigation tool and the first with built-in support for 
mobile and wireless computing, provided by Digital's RoamAbout 
Mobile IP.  It is also the first to provide an infrastructure for 
client/server applications being developed for multivendor 
enterprise networks by including the runtime licenses for 
ObjectBroker, Digital's CORBA-compliant object request broker 
software; DCE, Digital's OSF-standard Distributed Computing 
Environment; and DECmessageQ, Digital's industry-leading message 
queuing software.  Applications developed with these popular 
client/server tools now can be deployed on any PATHWORKS client 
without adding incremental software or incurring additional costs. 

Wider Database Access 

     Digital has added three new gateways to its ACCESSWORKS family 
for managing database access and integration.  The new ACCESSWORKS 
DB Integrator Gateways running on DEC OSF/1 and OpenVMS AXP 
platforms will extend access from 9 to 66 databases on popular 
industry hardware platforms such as IBM, Hewlett-Packard, and Sun 
host systems. The ACCESSWORKS DB Integrator Gateway for SequeLink 
extends read-write access to a range of databases such as DB/400, 
INFORMIX, CA-Ingres, Interbase, and PROGRESS.  Users also can gain 
read access to the databases reachable by IBI's EDA/SQL software 
product with the DB Integrator Gateway for EDA/SQL, and to several 
popular PC databases through the ACCESSWORKS DB Integrator Gateway 
for PC Data.  Connecting new databases is virtually automatic when 
using ACCESSWORKS DB Integrator software, with minimal programming 
beyond routine installation. 

Software Licensing Simplified 

     Digital has replaced multiple pricing tiers with a structure 
based on customer computing environments:  workgroup, department, 
and enterprise.  Customers can use the same license across a broad 
range of Alpha AXP and VAX systems.  This significantly reduces the 
number of times customers need to upgrade licenses when 
reconfiguring or upgrading systems.  Digital will continue to offer 
customers a choice between capacity or user-based license types.  
These changes increase the license value, eliminate software costs 
as a barrier to configuring optimal solutions, and reduce customers' 
software lifecycle costs. 

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha AXP 
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together 
with industry-focused solutions from business partners, help 
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace. 
