                   DIGITAL EXPANDS DESKTOP FAMILY
                       WITH NEW CELEBRIS LINE


MAYNARD, MA -- September 5, 1994 --  Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced a major extension of its popular desktop PC 
offerings, with five new personal computer systems including 
powerful Pentium systems, a new naming convention, new packaging, 
new enclosures and a new start-up menu -- all designed to help PC 
users become more productive, more quickly. 

     "Today's announcement is the first step in a major fall PC 
product roll-out that will move Digital's PC business further 
towards its goal of becoming a top five PC company by the end of 
1995," said Bernhard Auer, vice president and general manager of 
Digital's PC Business Unit.

     "Digital is known for delivering quality-engineered PCs, with 
excellent price/performance and outstanding service and support," 
Auer added.  "With our fall initiative, we are extending our PC 
strategy beyond excellent technology, to significantly enhancing 
how people interact with their computers.  Digital is investing in 
making the experience of dealing with computers easier and more 
productive." 

Performance For Advanced Business Applications -- At The Right Price

     The new Digital Celebris desktop line is tailored for business 
professionals who need a customized and more powerful computing 
environment that is easily and quickly adaptable to meet their 
advanced business application needs. Those typical business 
environments include management reporting, financial analysis, 
accounting, market analysis and research, and desktop publishing.

     The new Digital Celebris line is designed to maximize 
productivity and efficiency through well-balanced systems design. 
The systems offer excellent price/performance through:

     o	powerful processors, including high-end i486 and Pentium 
        models;

     o	integrated features, such as Peripheral Component 
        Interconnect (PCI)/ISA bus architecture for overall faster 
        system performance and enhanced IDE for faster disk 
        performance; 

     o	8MB of standard system memory, expandable to 128MB; 

     o	a high-performance external cache of 256KB, expandable to 
        512KB on Pentium models;

     o	leading-edge S3 64-bit graphics capabilities, with 1MB of 
        built-in video memory, expandable to 2MB; and

     o	a "virtual window" through video drivers that keep two 
        full-screen windows open simultaneously, either 
        horizontally or vertically.

Enhancements For Advanced Productivity Through Ease of Use Initiatives

     "The new Celebris enclosures are designed with PC users, 
support personnel and our channels partners in mind," said Ray 
Weadock, vice president and general manager of the Americas, for 
Digital's Personal Computer Business Unit. "The Celebris easy-
access cabinet design makes configuring, upgrading and service 
faster and more cost-effective," he added.

     Other ease-of-use initiatives announced today include new 
packaging with a quick set-up guide; a built-in, easy-to-follow 
start-up menu; as well as Plug and Play and Microsoft Chicago-ready 
system design.

     The entire Celebris line is in compliance with the U.S. 
government's Energy Star power-conservation guidelines, making 
Digital's Celebris PCs 'easy' on the environment, as well as an 
energy-saving value for the customer. 

     System security figures prominently in each of the new 
Celebris desktops, and includes an external chassis keylock, 
keyboard password, diskette access control, hard-drive access 
control and multiple-level password protection. The new PC line 
also comes with Digital's worldwide service and support through a 
limited three-year warranty, including one year on site.

     Four of the five new models in the Digital Celebris line -- 
the Digital Celebris 466, 4100, 560 and 590 -- offer slimline 
enclosures. The Digital FP590 features a full-profile enclosure. 
U.S. list pricing starts at $1,949 for the Digital Celebris 466 
model and $2,199 for the Pentium-based Digital Celebris 560. The 
Celebris 466, 4100, 560 and 590 are beginning to ship in September. 
The Digital Celebris FP590 will be available in early October.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems. Digital's scalable Alpha AXP 
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together 
with industry-focused solutions from business partners, help 
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace.
