            DIGITAL SHIPS NEW WIRELESS LAN CAPABILITIES


 Wireless LAN Offerings Enhanced With Unique Cell-to-Cell Roaming,
  Improved SNMP Capabilities and Comprehensive Network OS Support


MAYNARD, MA -- September 6, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today extended the scope of its seamless network access strategy, 
as the company announced new wireless LAN capabilities for its 
RoamAbout product family.  The RoamAbout Access Point and RoamAbout 
PCMCIA Network Adapter now offer expanded functionality, including 
cell-to-cell roaming, enhanced SNMP management, and support for
additional network operating systems.

     Digital's RoamAbout products couple the freedom of wireless 
communications with integrated LAN connectivity.  They offer 
improved access in dynamic business environments, flexibility in 
difficult wiring situations and simplified connectivity in 
temporary networking situations.

     The RoamAbout Access Point is a bridge between existing LANs 
and wireless DOS-based portables and desktop computers.  It 
operates in conjunction with the RoamAbout PCMCIA Network Adapter 
to enable wireless access to information on wire-based LANs.  Both 
the credit card-sized adapter and the RoamAbout Access Point are 
compatible with Digital's WaveLAN wireless network interface for
desktop PCs.

     The RoamAbout products offer a unique cell-to-cell roaming 
capability.  Each RoamAbout Access Point defines a connectivity 
'cell' with a diameter of up to 800 feet; users within that cell 
access the LAN connected to the RoamAbout Access Point as if they 
were connected directly.  Multiple RoamAbout Access Points work 
together to maintain users' network connections as they move 
between cells and throughout a building.

     "This announcement underscores Digital's strategy of providing 
seamless network access across an enterprise," noted Elaine 
Hodgdon, Digital's Internetworking marketing manager, "whether 
users are at a desktop processor and physically wired to the 
network...or using a personal digital assistant (PDA) while roaming 
across the plant floor.  Our new RoamAbout family is especially
innovative because it is the first high-performance wireless 
product to permit roaming across connectivity cells.  Today's 
mobile users are finally free to concentrate on running their 
business and not worry about network connectivity."  Digital's 
RoamAbout Access Point is particularly distinctive in that it 
permits deployment either on a standalone basis or as an integral 
part of Digital's DEChub family of modular, intelligent hubs.

     RoamAbout products also offer improved management 
functionality through a built-in SNMP management agent.  This 
enhancement permits RoamAbout components to be managed by SNMP 
systems, including Digital's HUBwatch and POLYCENTER/Netview for 
DEC OSF/1 AXP.

     Digital has also enhanced RoamAbout products' support of 
industry-standard drivers, such as NDIS/ODI.  They are now 
completely compatible with Netware, LAN Manager, PATHWORKS and 
other PC network operating systems.

     RoamAbout products have been deployed creatively to solve 
problems in many industries, including healthcare.  At a major 
Florida hospital, doctors and nurses rely on RoamAbout Access 
Points deployed throughout the hospital to access and update 
patient records with PDAs.  Hospital personnel benefit from the
technology because they are free to move about the hospital during 
their rounds with full access to key patient information.

     Digital is committed to providing leading edge solutions for 
mobile and wireless networking through a broad portfolio of 
products.  The company is participating in the development of the 
802.11 wireless standard, and has designed its RoamAbout Access 
Point to support it.  

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha AXP 
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together 
with industry-focused solutions from business partners, help
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace.
                                ####

