          DIGITAL ANNOUNCES ALL-IN-1 FOR ALPHA AXP SYSTEMS,
          ENHANCED TEAMLINKS, INTEGRATION WITH LOTUS NOTES


MAYNARD, Mass. -- September 12, 1994 -- Digital Equipment 
Corporation today announced the immediate availability of the 
ALL-IN-1 Office Server software on Digital's Alpha AXP systems 
running the OpenVMS operating system.  Also available today is an 
expanded suite of applications for the TeamLinks Office product for 
Microsoft Windows and Macintosh users, and enterprise electronic
mail services for users of Lotus Notes software.

     The addition of Alpha AXP support for ALL-IN-1 increases 
performance, lowers cost of ownership and protects the investments 
of more than five million current ALL-IN-1 users.  The office 
groupware now runs on OpenVMS based Alpha AXP and VAX servers 
across widely distributed enterprise networks.

     Microsoft Windows and Macintosh users can now take advantage 
of an enhanced TeamLinks Office suite of client applications that 
work with Alpha AXP and VAX servers using the ALL-IN-1 Office 
Server and Digital's DEC MAILworks server.  The TeamLinks Office 
product now includes Calendar Manager scheduling software and DEC 
VTX electronic library software in addition to electronic mail, 
routing and conferencing applications.  The TeamLinks client/server
workgroup computing solution is now more affordable and easier to 
buy.

     Users of Lotus Notes on Microsoft Windows can now enjoy the 
benefits of either the ALL-IN-1 or DEC MAILworks enterprise 
electronic mail capabilities.  A new service offering replaces the 
Lotus Notes mail function with the TeamLinks Mail for Windows 
client application.

The Most Widely Used Integrated Office Software Adds Alpha AXP Power

     ALL-IN-1 Office Server version 3.1, Digital's enterprise 
workgroup system for networked terminals, PCs, and Macintosh 
computers, is now available on OpenVMS Alpha AXP systems, offering 
improved performance and lower cost of ownership.

     ALL-IN-1 software delivers enterprise groupware applications 
and services such as mail, conferencing, shared filing, word 
processing, group scheduling, system management and administration.  
Alpha AXP support enables users to gain increased computing power 
as they progress to the next generation of client/server computing 
while protecting their investments in OpenVMS applications.  
Companies can continue to provide ALL-IN-1 software to their
existing video terminal users and workgroups on PC local area 
networks as well as workgroups with Alpha AXP systems.

     ALL-IN-1 software combined with the TeamLinks suite of 
enterprise groupware applications helps customers maximize the 
productivity of their Windows and Macintosh desktops, providing a 
cost-effective transition from time-sharing to client/server 
computing.  The ALL-IN-1 mail server has been redesigned for 
improved throughput and full compliance to the X.400 electronic
mail standard, for interoperability with other industry standard 
mail systems.

     ALL-IN-1 version 3.1 software is available immediately and 
pricing starts at $199 per video terminal user and $99 per user as 
a server to TeamLinks clients.  Other options, system 
configurations, and volume discounts are available.

New Service Integrates Enterprise Mail with Lotus Notes

     Today's announcement includes integration of TeamLinks Mail 
for Windows with Lotus Notes -- bringing TeamLinks and Digital Mail 
Services to Lotus Notes users.  Lotus Notes users gain the benefits 
of either the ALL-IN-1 or DEC MAILworks mail environment. The 
TeamLinks Mail client application will be automatically invoked 
when a Lotus Notes user mails a note.  In addition, the TeamLinks 
Mail inbox will identify a Lotus Notes attachment which has been
received and will automatically launch the Lotus Notes application.  
The service is available this month and pricing is dependent on 
installation requirements.

TeamLinks Mail Offers New Messaging Integration, Functionality

     Digital's announcement of enhanced TeamLinks Mail for 
Macintosh version 2.1 and TeamLinks Mail for Windows version 2.1 
includes new integration support for messaging interfaces.  Initial 
support of the  Microsoft messaging applications programming 
interface is available for the Windows product, while the Macintosh 
version now supports Apple Computer PowerTalk mail technology.

     The TeamLinks file cabinet now provides enhanced file sharing, 
improved performance, and new integration support for Microsoft 
Word version 6.0 and Microsoft Excel version 5.0 applications.
The new TeamLinks for Macintosh version can now be integrated with 
Digital's LinkWorks groupware product.  Both versions now support 
DEC MAILworks for DEC OSF/1 servers.  Version 2.1 of TeamLinks Mail 
products are available immediately and pricing has been lowered
to $55 per user with volume discounts available.

Calendar Manager Supports Alpha AXP Servers, Included with 
TeamLinks Office

     The Calendar Manager group scheduling client application from
Russell Information Sciences is now included with the TeamLinks 
Office product. It now supports Alpha AXP servers running the 
OpenVMS and DEC OSF/1 operating systems.  ALL-IN-1 users with Alpha 
AXP systems can take advantage of the robust group and resource 
scheduling capabilities of Calendar Manager software and its 
integration with Digital's ALL-IN-1 and TeamLinks Office solutions.

     Calendar Manager software supports video terminals, PCs 
running Microsoft DOS and Windows, Macintosh, OpenVMS AXP, OpenVMS 
VAX, DEC OSF/1, and NetWare platforms.  With a special introductory 
offer, the new Calendar Manager software is priced starting at 
$2100 per server with volume discounts available.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open  
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated  
worldwide information systems. Digital's scalable Alpha AXP  
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together  
with industry-focused solutions from business partners, help  
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace.  
