            DIGITAL EXPANDS ITS INTEGRATED SWITCHING AND
        ACCESS CAPABILITIES WITH RELEASE OF NETWORK PRODUCTS


ATLANTA, GA -- September 12, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
maintains its leadership role in the converging market for network 
switching and access with its announcement today of new, high-
performance network switches, servers and routers.  The new products 
dramatically enhance corporate connectivity, ranging from workgroup 
networking to enterprise-wide computing.

     "There are three important functions that are demanded by 
network users--hubbing, routing and switching," according to Dr. 
Laurence Walker, vice president and general manager of Digital's 
Network Product Business, "and the three are converging into a 
single, seamless product set.  This announcement demonstrates
Digital's momentum in the converging market, with a comprehensive 
set of offerings that enables easy connectivity across an entire 
organization."

Switching Products

     Digital's networking product strategy brings the benefits of 
high-performance switching to a range of network applications.  
Digital switches can connect multiple, high-performance personal 
computers, workstations and servers on a single LAN, as well as 
interconnect multiple desktop and departmental LANs into a high-
performance corporate backbone.

     Digital's new switches extend customers' flexibility in 
configuring and evolving their networks, complementing its award-
winning GIGAswitch/FDDI and DECswitch 900EF products.  Together, 
these switches offer network managers a wide range of high-
performance network solutions.

     The new DECswitch 900EE is a full-performance, store-and-
forward Ethernet switch for department-level connectivity.  The 
DECswitch 900EE dramatically improves network performance, providing 
high-speed access among multiple Ethernet LANs and backbones.  The 
DECswitch 900EE combines 'full-speed' switching with standards-
based, true 'store-and-forward' functionality, ensuring data 
integrity as well as high performance.  The DECswitch 900EE can also 
be easily upgraded to support multiprotocol routing capabilities.

     Digital targets its PEswitch 900TX at the emerging desktop 
switching market. This multiport Ethernet switch delivers low-cost, 
dedicated 10 Mb/s bandwidth to each port.  These 'personalized 
Ethernets' can in turn be switched at full speed to an FDDI link 
for high-performance desktop and/or server connections.  The 
PEswitch 900TX supports full IEEE-compliant Ethernet-FDDI 
translation and IP packet fragmentation for robust, high-performance 
switching.  The performance of desktop connections can be 
selectively upgraded with the PEswitch 900TX, at a cost that is 
significantly lower than other high-speed technologies.

     The DECswitch 900EE and the PEswitch 900TX are unique in that 
they can be deployed in either stand-alone ('rack and stack') 
configurations, as well as in a DEChub 900 Multi Switch.  The two 
new switches provide comprehensive filtering capabilities, 
encompassing source address, destination address and protocol
type.  Digital's entire switch family can be managed from HUBwatch, 
a low-cost, graphical SNMP management application available on a 
choice of PC and enterprise management platforms.

Access Products

     Digital offers a family of access products that provide 
seamless connectivity from remote sites to the enterprise network.  
Digital's product set includes connectivity solutions for the 
traveling professional and at-home worker, as well as branch offices 
and regional sites.

     The enhanced DECserver family provides networking solutions for 
client/server computing, interconnecting remote desktop and laptop 
devices running various operating systems and network protocols.  
Composed of the DECserver 90M, DECserver 700 and DECserver 900TM 
products, the product set provides full remote user access to Novell 
IPX, AppleTalk and IP servers.  Users now have full remote node 
functionality within all these environments through a single 
DECserver.

     The DECbrouter 90, developed jointly with Cisco Systems, is a 
multiprotocol internetworking solution for linking Ethernet networks 
across a wide area.  This announcement features an upgraded hardware 
platform incorporating expanded memory.  Designed to deliver the 
industry's best price/performance in its class, the DECbrouter 90 
runs the full suite of Cisco's multiprotocol routing software at an 
attractively low price point.  It will continue to be a cost-
effective solution for expanding installed networks that are based 
on Cisco backbone routers.

     Since its introduction in 1993, the DECwanrouter 90 has been 
especially popular because of its low cost and support for TCP/IP, 
DECnet and OSI.  Already one of the most cost-effective multi-
protocol routers on the market today, Digital has lowered its price 
by 27% to $1,450.  In addition, the DECwanrouter 90 now supports 
Novell IPX environments.

     Digital is also expanding its DECwanrouter family with the 
introduction of the DECwanrouter 90EW.  This unit provides 
cost-effective connections of small Ethernet LANs to regional or 
backbone sites, across wide-area services such as leased line, 
dial-up and X.25 through two WAN ports.  The new DECwanrouter 90EW
supports TCP/IP, IPX, OSI and DECnet, and features flash memory that 
enables easy software upgrade and configuration.  Digital also 
designed its new router to accept an ISDN card, which will be 
announced shortly.

     "From the customer standpoint," noted William Maro, Digital's 
vice president of network product marketing and engineering, 
"Digital offers a complete line of scalable switches and access 
products that deliver connectivity to the desktop, within the 
department and across the enterprise.  Our innovative building-block
approach encourages redeployment of modules as needs evolve, easing 
evolution while preserving network investments.  Digital's product 
introductions today continue to expand our customers' networking 
options.  Digital continues to lead the industry in delivering 
high-performing, scalable networks to the converging market."

Pricing and volume availability for these products is as follows:

