              DIGITAL AND FRONTIER SOFTWARE COLLABORATE
           ON COMPREHENSIVE NETWORK PERFORMANCE MONITORING


MAYNARD, MA -- September 19, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
and Frontier Software, Inc., today announced their intent to 
continue joint development on new products and features for network 
performance monitoring. The DECpacketprobe 900RR, announced today, 
is a token ring version of the DECpacketprobe for the DEChub 900 
MultiSwitch which supports RFC 1513 for Token Ring. 

     New features for existing products, the DECpacketprobe 90 and 
PROBEwatch, are being announced today. For DECpacketprobe 90, these 
include support for remote out-of-band management using SLIP, and 
automatic reloading of configuration parameters after a power loss. 
Among the new PROBEwatch features are multisegment views of the 
network for better analysis and support for token ring. These 
enhancements extend Digital's leadership position for RMON in the 
hub.

     In addition, Digital and Frontier are collaborating on 
embedding Frontier's RMON agent on a multiport Ethernet agent module 
for the DEChub 900 MultiSwitch. With this product, users will be 
able to monitor the multiple LAN segments on the DEChub 900 
MultiSwitch with a single module. 

     The original agreement between the two companies called for 
Digital's products to benefit from Frontier's enhancements to their 
NETscout products. Digital was one of the first vendors to 
incorporate full RMON into a hub module. The DECpacketprobe 90 is 
packaged in the award-winning unique DEChub 90 format, which allows 
it to work in any of Digital's hubs or standalone anywhere on the 
LAN. 

     "We wanted to make RMON an integral piece of our DEChub product 
set," said Bill Maro, vice president, networks product marketing 
and engineering. "Our customers demand increased manageability of 
their networks; by embedding standards-based RMON, we can provide 
the cost-effective remote monitoring that is necessary for ensuring 
high availability of enterprise networks," Since hubs are strategic 
network elements where LAN segments come together, they represent 
ideal monitoring points.

     Narendra Popat, president of Frontier, said "With Frontier's 
RMON technology integrated into Digital's advanced networking 
products, Digital's customers can both build and manage state-of-
the-art enterprise networks. We feel that Digital's thorough 
evaluation and selection of Frontier as its partner for RMON 
technology is a strong endorsement of our extensive product 
capabilities and RMON technology leadership."

     Frontier Software located in Tewksbury, Massachusetts, and 
founded in 1984, is a technology leader in the development of the 
RMON standard and RMON based distributed diagnostic systems.  In 
1993 Frontier was the first to deliver RMON management for WANs.
In 1989, Frontier introduced the industry's first distributed LAN 
analyzer product for Ethernet and Token Ring networks.
Frontier is an active member of the IETF RMON committee and has been 
a key contributor to establishing this new management standard (RFC 
1271) for distributed LAN diagnostics.  Frontier's products include 
the NETscout family of intelligent SNMP/RMON LAN/WAN Probes and 
management console analysis software tools.  The family was 
introduced in 1992 and was the first RMON based distributed 
diagnostic product line available in the industry.  Frontier 
markets the NETscout family on a worldwide basis through VARs, 
system integrators, and OEMs, as well as directly to major end 
users.  

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha AXP 
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together 
with industry-focused solutions from business partners, help 
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace.
