              DIGITAL NAMED AS NOVELL'S FIRST WORLDWIDE
                    SOFTWARE MAINTENANCE PROVIDER


 ... Tailored support for individual Novell sites now available ...


MAYNARD, Mass. -- September 19, 1994 -- Novell NetWare users world-
wide can now enjoy the benefits of "unbundled" one-step shopping for 
Novell NetWare 3 and 4 software upgrade services under terms of an 
agreement naming Digital Equipment Corporation as Novell's first 
worldwide software maintenance provider.

     Digital will now manage the procurement of the upgrades, 
documentation and media of a Novell site, making it easier for 
NetWare users to help keep their Novell client/server environments 
software current.  In addition, customers will see a marked 
reduction in the administrative and product upgrade costs 
traditionally associated with maintenance of their software.

     In an industry first, Digital has unbundled software upgrades, 
giving customers a way to better align their costs with their site 
licensing and documentation requirements.  Users can now purchase 
the exact number of licenses, media and documentation they need for 
NetWare products and solutions.

     This latest agreement further extends a series of ongoing 
product, service and support partnerships between the two companies, 
including Digital's recent participation in Novell's Authorized 
Service Center (NASC) program. Several features of this latest 
partnership build on these previous agreements.  Foremost is Digital's 
access to Novell software products before their release, ensuring 
Novell users worldwide of up-to-the-moment technical support from 
Digital for their NetWare environments.

     "We are delighted that Novell has once again turned to Digital 
to deliver support services to its worldwide customer base.  This 
latest agreement will allow NetWare sites to take advantage of our 
expertise in Network Service and Support, helping us help them run 
more efficient multivendor sites," said John Rando, Digital vice 
president, Digital Multivendor Customer Services.

     "We see a growing demand from our customers worldwide for 
services that help them manage their increasingly complex multi-
vendor client/server environments," said Jim T. Sullivan, vice 
president, Worldwide OEM Sales for Novell. "Naming Digital as our 
first worldwide provider of software maintenance services is part of 
our ongoing effort to meet the global service needs of our NetWare 
customers.  Digital has been successfully providing support to our 
customers in a variety of capacities for a number of years.  When 
looking for a support partner that could globally deliver timely and 
targeted technical support solutions to our NetWare customers, we 
knew we could count on Digital."

The three key features of the agreement are:

     -	New Version Licensing (NVLS), which provides the right to 
        use all new versions of the product that are released.  
        Users will automatically receive upgrade license rights for 
        the quantity of licensed products for which they have 
        purchased coverage;

     -	Media Subscription Service, which provides media upgrades as 
        soon as Novell releases new versions of NetWare; and

     -	Documentation Subscription Service, whereby Digital will 
        provide full new version hard copy documentation upgrades as 
        soon as Novell releases them.

     Digital's support is available for all of Novell's language 
versions.  Customers can purchase these service offerings through 
both direct and indirect sales channels.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha AXP 
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together 
with industry-focused solutions from business partners, help 
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace.
