             HUGHES SELECTS DIGITAL'S ALPHA AXP SERVERS
         AS STRATEGIC PLATFORM FOR MULTI-MILLION DOLLAR MOVE
                   TO OPEN CLIENT/SERVER COMPUTING


... Choice Based on Standards, Performance, Flexibility, Support ...


MAYNARD, MA -- September 20, 1994 -- Furthering its progress toward 
integrated global information technology (IT) systems, reduced costs 
and improved time-to-market, Hughes Aircraft has chosen Digital 
Equipment Corporation's 64-bit Alpha AXP servers as the standard 
platform for its Enterprise Server Project. 

     The contract, estimated at $20 million over the next two years, 
calls for the use of Digital's Alpha AXP servers running the DEC 
OSF/1 operating system, Digital's implementation of the UNIX 
operating system. The servers will support a wide variety of 
business-critical applications including manufacturing resource 
planning (MRP), product data management (PDM), database, data 
warehouse, and communications applications. 

     "We performed an intensive search for the best server platform 
to support our traditional defense business and our aggressive entry 
into the commercial market," said James Woods, chief information 
officer for Hughes. "Digital's Alpha AXP platform was chosen based 
on price/performance, 64-bit scalability for future expansion, and 
standards compliance."

     "Digital not only had the standards-based technology, but also 
the network management, administration configuration and warranties 
to support it," added Woods.

     Hughes' Enterprise Server Program is part of a major business 
reengineering plan. The plan includes development of flexible 
systems able to adapt with changing business needs through 
downsizing from centralized mainframe applications to distributed 
applications across an open client/server environment.

     Digital's Alpha AXP servers, including the Digital 2100 Server, 
are already installed as part of the program in Hughes' Fullerton 
and Long Beach, California, locations. 

     Digital's 2100 Server Model A500MP offers the industry's best 
price/performance for mid-range servers. It is the first in a new 
family of RISC-based, symmetric multiprocessing departmental servers 
-- combining the benefits of large-system features with small system 
advantages. The system supports between one and four 190 MHz Alpha 
AXP processors and large amounts of storage and memory, combined 
with the low cost, openness and flexibility of PCI and EISA buses.

     Hughes is an integrated company in the automotive electronics; 
aerospace and defense electronics; commercial electronics; and 
commercial electronics markets.

