Corporation today announced a new agreement with Acudata, Inc., an 
electronic manufacturers' representative covering Texas, Oklahoma, 
Louisiana and Arkansas, to market Digital's Alpha AXPvme line of 
64-bit RISC-based single board computers and realtime software.  
Houston-based Acudata -- a well-known sales and marketing 
organization founded in 1981 -- specializes in providing 
microcomputer boards and systems, graphics and image processors, 
communications products and test/measurement equipment to customers 
in military/aerospace, medical science, simulation, communications 
and graphics industries.  The announcement was made at the Air 
Traffic Controllers Conference, which opened here today at the 
Hyatt Regency Crystal City Convention Center.

      Under the terms of the agreement, Acudata will market the 
following Digital products: the Alpha AXPvme line of 64-bit RISC 
PCI-based VME SBCs; the Alpha AXPpci 33 PCI-based PC motherboards; 
the VxWorks for Alpha AXP realtime embedded software, and; the DEC 
OSF/1 UNIX operating system with realtime extensions. 

      According to Bill Armitage, Vice President of Digital's 
Embedded and Realtime Products Group, "The agreement with Acudata 
is part of Digital's channel strategy for embedded and realtime 
products.  Our goal is to create a broad geographic base of 
partnerships with well-regarded manufacturers' representatives 
specializing in industries where customers need the high-
performance characteristics of our 64-bit Alpha AXP technologies.

      "Acudata's market base closely tracks Digital's expertise in 
the VMEbus and realtime arena," Armitage continued.  "Through their 
long-term association with principals and clients in the embedded 
and realtime markets, Acudata's experience and knowledge closely 
parallels Digital's sales and marketing needs."

      Led by industry veterans Samuel Gougenheim and Daryl Barnaby, 
Acudata possesses strong technical and sales credentials, with 
experience in private industry, design, sales and sales management 
capacities.  "We are delighted to add Digital to our growing roster 
of  leading vendors," said Gougenheim.  "Digital's industry-leading 
technologies and comprehensive service and support programs present 
a compelling sales message to customers interested in long-lived, 
high-performance VMEbus solutions."

      Founded in 1981, privately-held Acudata is an electronic 
manufacturers' representative with offices in Houston, Dallas, 
Austin and Tulsa.  With approximately $20 million in annual sales, 
Acudata provides a broad range of marketing services to some of the 
VMEbus industry's top companies, including Greenspring Computers, 
Electronic Solutions, Rockwell Network Systems, Spectrum Signal 
Processing, Vigra, and VMETRO.

