  ...Digital Combines the Versatility of the VME Architecture with
           the High-Performance Characteristics of PCI...


CRYSTAL CITY, Virginia -- September 20, 1994 --  Digital Equipment 
Corporation today announced a PCI to VME Adapter that will allow 
devices on the VMEbus to interact transparently with the host Alpha 
AXP system, as if they are located directly on the PCI native bus:  
this allows all PCI-based Alpha AXP client and server systems to be 
used with VME devices.  The announcement was made at the Air Traffic 
Controllers Conference, which opened here today at the Hyatt Regency 
Crystal City Convention Center.

     According to Tom Rarich, VME Marketing Manger in Digital's 
Embedded and Realtime Products Group, "The PCI-VME Adapter will 
allow our partners to enhance the value of their Alpha AXP systems.  
By combining the processing power of Alpha AXP, the industry-proven 
flexibility of the VME architecture, and the next-generation 
performance characteristics of PCI, Digital's customers will be 
able to create optimal systems to run their compute-intensive 
applications."    

     Among the highlights of the PCI-VME Adapter are:  access to 
over 4,000 VMEbus peripherals and controllers; industry-leading I/O 
performance; memory-mapped support; "Endian" byte-swapping hardware; 
an onboard DMA engine; and a consistent software interface with 
other Digital VME adapters, under the Digital Realtime DEC OSF/1 and 
OpenVMS operating systems.
 
PCI-VME Adapter Provides A Seamless ALPHA AXP to VMEbus Integration

     "The PCI-VME Adapter supplies a seamless Alpha AXP PCI to 
VMEbus integration," said Rarich.  "Utilizing memory-mapping 
processes, VME address space and memory cells are fully-accessible 
to the host software -- while host address space and cells are 
accessible to VME devices."  In this way, most required I/O 
transactions occur as if the VMEbus were built into the host system.

     Since the PCI-VME Adapter card is viewed as an integral 
processor on the VMEbus, the Alpha AXP system can function as either 
a coprocessor or as the VMEbus bus master processor.  Consequently, 
the Alpha AXP host system can directly control and monitor a wide 
variety of VME bus cards and high-performance processors -- 
eliminating the need for an additional VMEbus system controller.

     The Adapter consists of a VME (6U) card, a PC style (edge 
connector) PCI card, and a cable up to 25 feet long that connects 
the PCI system to the VME chassis.

Software Porting Without Modifications ... Applications To Meet 
Market Needs ...

     According to Rarich, all existing hardware modules designed to 
the popular VMEbus standard can be utilized without modification 
with the PCI to VME Adapter connecting them to an Alpha AXP host.  
Digital OSF/1 and OpenVMS operating system extensions for the 
Adapter are included with the Adapter hardware, and porting of 
software device drivers to the Digital OSF/1 or OpenVMS operating 
systems is fast and easy. 

     The PCI-VME Adapter supports VME devices that are popular in 
applications such as industrial automation, medical imaging, 
real-time controls, image and signal processing, and seismic data 
acquisition and analysis.

A Bridge To The Future

     "The Digital PCI-VME Adapter is an open bridge to the future," 
Rarich concluded.  "Our customers will now be able to access the 
incredible breadth of existing VMEbus options from their Digital 
Alpha AXP PCI-based systems, and to combine them with high-
performance PCI options on the same system for industry-leading 
performance and versatility."

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha AXP 
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together 
with industry-focused solutions from business partners, help 
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace.
