QPI Sales, Digital continues to expand its fast-growing presence in 
the embedded and realtime market," said Bill Armitage, Vice 
President of Digital's Embedded and Realtime Products Group.  "QPI 
Sales represents a particularly strong fit for Digital:  their 
long-term VMEbus expertise and established presence in the process 
control, military/aerospace and communications industries will 
ensure successful growth for both companies." 

     James Carver, founder of QPI Sales, was enthusiastic about 
Digital's industry-leading VME product lines.  "Supported by 
Digital's UNIX operating system, DEC OSF/1, and the VxWorks for 
Alpha AXP realtime development interface, Digital's Alpha AXPvme 
board line is a powerful competitor in the OEM space.  Digital's 
leading-edge technology -- combined with the Company's excellent OEM 
support programs and worldwide reputation -- represents an 
outstanding addition to QPI Sales' portfolio of products."

     With offices throughout Southern California, QPI Sales provides 
a select group of manufacturers with senior-level sales and 
marketing programs.  Specializing in high-quality, state-of-the-art 
product lines, QPI Sales has established long-term partnerships with 
manufacturers such as Xycom, CMC/Rockwell, Omnibyte and Titan, and 
touts military and commercial accounts ranging from AP Labs, General 
Dynamics, McDonnell Douglas and Hughes Aircraft to the Sony 
Corporation.

