   ...VADSworks Will Provide Front-End Ada Development Environment
  To Digital's VxWorks For Alpha AXP Embedded Realtime Software...


CRYSTAL CITY, Virginia -- September 20, 1994 -- Fulfilling the 
increasing demand for complete, high-performance embedded and 
realtime solutions from its growing customer base of Original 
Equipment Manufacturers (OEMs) in the military sector, Digital 
Equipment Corporation today announced an agreement with Rational 
Software Corporation to port the VADSworks compilation system for 
UNIX and realtime embedded systems on Alpha AXP 64-bit RISC 
platforms and VMEbus single board computers.  VADSworks is part of 
Rational's VADS family of compilers and cross compilers for 
high-performance embedded applications.  VADSworks will be used as 
the front end of Digital's VxWorks for Alpha AXP operating system, 
the industry-leading realtime software which runs on Alpha 64-bit 
RISC VMEbus single board computers.  As part of the Alpha AXP Ada 
solution, Rational will also provide VADSself and VADScross, two 
Ada compiler systems, as complementary options to the VADSworks 
solution.  The announcement was made at the Air Traffic Controllers 
Conference, which opened here today at the Hyatt Regency Crystal 
City convention Center.

     Under the terms of the agreement, Rational will port the 
VADSworks solution to the  Alpha AXP 64-bit RISC platforms and 
VxWorks for Alpha AXP software.  Rational is adopting Alpha AXP as 
its Ada development platform of choice -- all forthcoming VADSworks 
solutions will be released first on Alpha AXP.  OEM customers may 
purchase the VADSworks/Alpha AXP solutions from the Rational sales 
channel.

     "This agreement represents the tremendous progress Alpha AXP 
has made in the military OEM sector as well as Digital's commitment 
to extend military/embedded and Ada applications to peak performance 
levels," said Steve Hargrave, of Digital's Embedded and Realtime 
Products Group.  "Furthermore, our agreement with Rational allows us 
to fully support our growing base of military OEMs, including 
Raytheon, Westinghouse and AEON Systems, with the most comprehensive 
Ada product line available today."  And, with Alpha AXP positioned 
as the VADSworks development platform of choice, continued Hargrave, 
customers can access the latest technologies.

     Tom Smith, the Strategic Account Manager for Santa Clara, 
CA-based Rational, states that the porting agreement will provide 
Rational with access to large, worldwide OEM customers as well as a 
head start in the burgeoning VMEbus/PCI (Peripheral Component 
Interface) solutions market.

     Digital, the first vendor to ship commercially-available 
PCI-based single board computers, also markets one of the industry's 
highest-performing VMEbus single board computer product line.

     Paul Zorfass, an industry analyst covering embedded systems and 
software for International Data Corporation (IDC), a Framingham, 
MA-based market research firm, believes the agreement will encourage 
several military OEMs to move to Alpha AXP-based systems.  "Having 
VADSworks as a high-performance Ada front-end for VxWorks for Alpha 
AXP systems will enable existing VADSworks users to easily port 
their applications to the Alpha architecture.  They can thus take 
advantage of the Alpha AXP superior performance in both the host and 
target domains.

     VADSworks is the result of a joint development effort by 
Rational and Wind River Systems to integrate Rational's VADS 
compilation system with Wind River's Real-time Network Operating 
System, known as the VxWorks product.  Digital ported the VxWorks 
5.1 software to Alpha AXP and added functional enhancements, 
including a full 64-bit RISC implementation.  VADSworks will be 
available on both Alpha AXP hosts and targets in November 1994.  
Prices will begin at $35,000.

Special Head Start Program Offered To Military OEMs

     For Ada embedded developers that wish to move to an Alpha AXP 
platform immediately, the VADSself native compiler for Alpha AXP is 
available immediately.  Military and other OEMs can begin 
development immediately with VADSself on an Alpha AXP workstation, 
and move to the language-compatible VADSworks when it becomes 
available in November.  

     "This Head Start Program will jump-start our military OEM 
market efforts very aggressively," said Hargrave. For more 
information on the Program, please contact Rational at 408-496-3600.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha AXP 
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together 
with industry-focused solutions from business partners, help 
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace.
