          DIGITAL EQUIPMENT ANNOUNCES NEW HIGH-PERFORMANCE
                BACKUP SUBSYSTEMS FOR THE SUN MARKET


 StorageWorks DLT Subsystem Expands Tape Backup Options for Sun Users


MAYNARD, Mass. -- September 27, 1994 -- Digital Equipment 
Corporation today expanded its portfolio of storage solutions for 
the Sun Microsystems workstation environment with the StorageWorks 
TZ87N DLT (Digital Linear Tape) subsystem.  The StorageWorks DLT 
subsystem for Sun leads the industry in performance and reliability 
for tape back-up, archival, and HSM solutions.  The product offers 
up to 10GB (20GB compressed) of storage capacity, with high-
reliability for high-duty cycle usage.  With the addition of the DLT
subsystem, StorageWorks now offers Sun users the ability to match 
their performance requirements with a broad range of tape 
technologies including 4mm, 8mm, and DLT drives.

     "Sun workstation users in commercial environments are 
increasingly demanding data availability and performance," stated 
Penny Scharfman, Digital's StorageWorks marketing manager for the 
Sun market.  "Digital's StorageWorks DLT subsystem now offers Sun 
customers two-to-three times the performance of 4mm and 8mm for 
their backup/restore, archival and HSM requirements."

     Kirby Wadsworth, manager, Digital's StorageWorks product 
marketing, added, "StorageWorks' expanded offerings for Sun users 
reinforces Digital's commitment to provide the industry's broadest 
range of modular, scalable, and cost-effective storage solutions for 
multiple computing platforms and environments.  In the Sun market, 
Digital provides more storage solutions than any other vendor, with 
RAID, disk, tape, and solid-state disk offerings."

     DLT's advanced linear tape path design provides exceptional 
durability and data integrity, along with the ability to back up 
large amounts of data.  The StorageWorks DLT subsystem for SunOS and 
Solaris offers:

     -	Unattended high performance back-up -- up to 150 MB per 
        minute

     -	Industry leading capacity -- up to 20 GB per DLT cartridge

     -	Reliable operation for maximum data availability in 
        high-duty cycle tape applications such as HSM

     -	Two configurations for maximum flexibility -- either a 
        StorageWorks 5.25-inch building block or a separate tabletop 
        enclosure

Pricing and Availability

     The StorageWorks TZ87N DLT subsystem for Sun is priced at 
$4,999 in either the StorageWorks building block or tabletop 
enclosure.  The product is available now from select value-added 
resellers (VARs), wholesale distributors and systems integrators.  
Call 1-800-STORWORK for more information.

     StorageWorks is a comprehensive family of disk, tape and 
optical storage subsystems, offering modular, competitively-priced, 
industry-standard solutions in customizable desktop, deskside and 
datacenter enclosures. StorageWorks products are available on multiple 
operating systems and hardware platforms, including Sun Microsystems 
workstations, Novell environments, and Digital workstations and midrange 
computers.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha AXP 
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together 
with industry-focused solutions from business partners, help
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace.
